>
> For this one, I can see a reason: {gasnu} refers to an actual event,
> while {curmi} is a counterfactual: x1 would allow x2 to happen in
> conditions x3.

But that's not the way to express counterfactuals in Lojban.
{mi ca'a curmi le nu ti farlu} means "I let this fall", not
"I would actually let this fall under certain conditions".
The conditions are the ambient conditions, just like with
any other predicate.

You could equally well argue that {gasnu} needs an x3 to say
"x1 would bring about x2 under conditions x3".

